Strict alignment: test a base once for a run of accesses through it (applies after perf-76).

Under JitRiscV64StrictAlign every access whose address the JIT cannot prove aligned tests that address
(andi + beqz), even when an access just before it in the same block tested the same base: the fields
of a struct passed by reference, the words of a buffer. On the Nethermind SP1 guest, 44% of the tests
left after perf-76 repeat one made earlier in the function.

Lowering now versions such runs before it lowers the blocks (VersionAlignmentChecks). For the run of
a block that holds the most tested accesses through one local, the block is split so the run is entered
through a single test of that local:

    prefix
    andi  t, base, size-1
    bnez  t, slow
    run                  ; base aligned: KnownAlignmentLog2 proves the accesses, no tests
  rest:
    ...
  slow:                  ; rarely run, out of line
    clone of run         ; every access keeps its test
    j     rest

The aligned run records the tested alignment as a fact of its block, which KnownAlignmentLog2 reads
for that local while the block is lowered. A run starts at a statement and ends at its last access; it
holds no store to the local (or the struct it is a field of) and only simple nodes (no calls, no struct
values), which the clone copies node for node. Values the run computes for the rest of a statement go
through temps. The prefix, the aligned run and the rest are searched again for other locals, and the
clones are capped at the node count of the method. ContainCheckIndir also clears the unaligned flag the
front end set (Unsafe.ReadUnaligned etc.) on an access whose address it proves aligned.

Nethermind stateless guest on SP1 (sp1-runner v6.6.0, master cd336c4ccc), on top of perf-76, cycles:
  block 26055159: 102,844,417 -> 101,351,395 (-1.45%), gas -0.59%
  block 26112793: 226,298,346 -> 222,697,765 (-1.59%), gas -0.74%
  geomean over 11 mainnet blocks: cycles -1.54%, gas -0.70%; outputs identical on all 11.
Clearing the front-end flag alone is -0.22% on both blocks. Only builds with JitRiscV64StrictAlign
change: the ZisK guest builds byte-identical.
Regression test: tools/tests/StrictAlignment/FastPath.

